<section class="page-intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Adoption guide</p>
  <h1 id="page-title">Bring in the foundation. Keep your project in charge.</h1>
  <p class="lede">The framework is designed to be vendored into a host repository. Start with the smallest integration that gives agents the context and gates they need.</p>
</section>

<section class="steps" aria-labelledby="quick-start">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Quick start</p>
    <h2 id="quick-start">A minimal submodule integration</h2>
  </div>
  <ol class="step-list">
    <li>
      <div class="step-number">01</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Add the foundation layer</h3>
        <p>Keep the framework at <code>vendor/conventional-agents/</code> so updates are explicit and the host repository remains the owner of project-specific rules.</p>
        <pre><code>git submodule add https://github.com/Tais-Den/conventional-agents.git vendor/conventional-agents
git submodule update --init</code></pre>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-number">02</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Write a small root stub</h3>
        <p>Point your agent runtime at the framework's role contract, integration guide, and session modes. Add project context in the host repository instead of copying the whole framework.</p>
        <pre><code># Agent Instructions

## Read First
- vendor/conventional-agents/guidelines/ROLE_CONTRACT.md
- vendor/conventional-agents/INTEGRATION.md
- vendor/conventional-agents/workflows/session-modes.md</code></pre>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-number">03</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Make precedence explicit</h3>
        <p>Host-repository rules sit above reusable guidance, while universal safety gates cannot be weakened. Record exceptions locally and keep the shared layer portable.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="pattern-grid" aria-labelledby="choose-pattern">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Choose a pattern</p>
    <h2 id="choose-pattern">Match the integration to the host repository.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="cards-2x2">
    <article class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-label">Recommended default</span><h3>Submodule + hybrid stub</h3><p>Use a submodule for the shared foundation and a short root file for project-specific context.</p></article>
    <article class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-label">Tool constraint</span><h3>Copy-in</h3><p>Use a recorded snapshot when a tool only reads root files or a submodule is not practical.</p></article>
    <article class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-label">Organization scale</span><h3>Consumer conventions</h3><p>Vendor organization-specific conventions as a sibling layer rather than embedding them upstream.</p></article>
    <article class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-label">High customization</span><h3>Fork and vendor</h3><p>Keep a fork explicit when the host needs durable changes that do not belong in the shared framework.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="callout callout-muted" aria-labelledby="integration-rule">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Integration rule</p>
    <h2 id="integration-rule">Strengthen shared gates if you need to. Do not silently weaken them.</h2>
  </div>
